    <briefdescription>
<para>Defines the <ref refid="classStore" kindref="compound">Store</ref>&apos;s single shared registry, lock and generation counter. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This file contains no functions. It only gives real storage to the three static variables that <ref refid="store_8hpp" kindref="compound">store.hpp</ref> declares: a map from a C++ type to its one shared object, a mutex protecting that map, and a counter used to refresh per-thread caches. The counter starts at 1 so that a brand-new thread, whose remembered value starts at 0, always performs a lookup the first time it asks for an object.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: These few definitions are the physical storage behind the service locator. Every call to <ref refid="classStore_1a0607fb3b583c06ca910ed6c9881e790c" kindref="member">Store::getObject()</ref>, <ref refid="classStore_1aaf81da54b109478891030b7e04653bad" kindref="member">Store::cachedObject()</ref> or <ref refid="classStore_1a2a4bfc0b18f2999216eda3067988cf57" kindref="member">Store::replaceObject()</ref> reads or changes these variables. Without this file the header would only declare names and the linker would report &quot;undefined reference&quot; errors. Tests also depend on the counter starting at 1, so a freshly installed fake is noticed on the very first cached lookup.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>None difficult here; this file only provides real storage (a &quot;definition&quot;) for names declared in the header.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
